# Short-Form Thumbnails — Not VOD Episodes

**Shorts are never VOD shows.** They are standalone vertical clips, not numbered episodes of a news/sports/Twitch Soup series.

## Thumbnail rules

**✅ Short-form thumbnails (`templateId: short-form`, `*-short` content types):**
- Clean frame pulled from the assembled video only
- No burned text: no EP badge, no episode number, no show name, no tagline ("Because the Light Was On", etc.)
- Custom YouTube thumb is set at publish time (often on mobile)

**✅ Allowed paths:**
- `generateShortFrameThumbnail()` — Gemini frame pick or plain FFmpeg fallback
- `POST /thumbnail-short` — portrait frame extract, scale/pad only

**❌ NEVER for shorts:**
- `generateThumbnail()` designed HTML/overlay templates (VOD episode branding)
- `drawtext` / `drawbox` overlays with show name, EP, or series tagline
- Falling back to long-form thumbnail templates when frame extract fails

**Long-form VOD** (`templateId: long-form`) may use designed templates with show chrome — that path does not apply to shorts.
